A||N||4||Haze_Performance||sail panel install??||||5||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||06-22-2000||04:57 AM||||I got my new sail panels and now its time to change them.I cracked my old drivers side one while pumping gas (leaning on the car). My question is can I just pry the old panel off without removing the entire panel??Is it just held on with tape?? (I dont care if I break up the old one) <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RACING_1.jpg"> <P>Mine are "Pontiac in Red", "Racing in Silver & White flag||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||06-22-2000||11:02 AM||||I would say remove the panel then remopve the plastic and replace then reinstall the panel. But I am sure some will say just rip the old plastic from the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-22-2000||11:13 AM||||I just removed the set from the Monkeymobile.  There are a couple of plug in clip things on/under the rear edge that I just popped out.  Unfortunately, there's also a clip with a hidden nut on the front bottom corner.  I tried to unscrew the nut, but for some reason, it wouldn't unscrew.  You can pull the panel out far enough just by popping the rear things loose to see what I'm talking about.  The only way to get to the nut in front is to remove the inner sail panel. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  You can still remove the panel by using a screwdriver to loosen the front clip from the panel.  If I could get my PIP to post anything other than the dancing frog, I'd post some pics to help explain what I'm talking about.  (BTW--I'm probably going to use the sail panels from the MM [they're plain] only because they don't have the same cracks in them that the originals do on the GA.  Someday I'll find a glass set from an '84, strip 'em and paint a real Grape Ape on.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||William||06-22-2000||12:23 PM||||I'm gonna be one of those other people Tom was talking about. When I got my replacment panels from Paul, I decided leave the plastic frames on the car. The process was easy! I used a wide putty knife to pry off the old panels. Then I used a razor blade to slowly remove the remaning sticky tape,(Worked fanatastic!). The removal process took about 15 minutes. I then painted the frames and installed the new panels!! I could not see ANY reason to remove the panels other than the fact that painting them would be a little easier. I'm glad I didn't remove mine and have to deal with the clips.<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||06-22-2000||01:32 PM||||Thanks guys. I like the last way best  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> . My panels are perfect (no need to paint). I know the right way would be to remove the entire panel. But I dont have the time right now.<P>Thanks for the replys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
